er, the claim also includes details about freshwater influx from melting ice sheets, permafrost carbon feedback, and specific risks of crossing a tipping point, which are not explicitly addressed in the quoted text. While UCAR is a credible source, it is an educational platform rather than a primary research outlet, and the quote only partially backs the full claim. Hence, a score of 0.8 is appropriate.', '{ocean,climate}', NULL, 'continental', 'measured', NULL);
