-reviewed paper itself, university news outlets typically maintain strong editorial standards and accurately represent the research. The quote directly backs the claim, lending it credibility. However, some specific numerical details in the claim (e.g., 22% deforestation threshold) are not explicitly in the quote, slightly reducing the source''s ability to establish the full claim without further verification. Overall, it is a credible secondary source deserving a high score but not the highest reserved for primary research.', '{forest,biosphere,climate}', NULL, 'planetary', 'measured', NULL);
